(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/config.asl#gatewayRouteEntries!" :text "returned table carries the undeclared-intent count")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#" :text "The gateway dispatch path: provider rows and plugins from the gateway config, then route (router.asl) -> endpoints (fleet.asl) -> pick (spillover) -> admission -> budget gate -> send (plugin) -> charge (budget.asl), one decision row per request.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#Serverless" :text "a scale-to-zero endpoint: how long a start may take, what one start is expected to cost (microUSD) and the budget unit it is charged to")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#Slot" :text "a configured endpoint with its live fleet state; price is microUSD per million tokens, the budget unit (adopted); polledMs throttles lifecycle status calls; deadlineMs ends a start's warm-up")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#Plan" :text "planWait parks a request on a serverless endpoint until it is warm or deadlineMs passes; cold means the endpoint still has to be started")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#LifecycleFamily" :text "a family turns one (:lifecycle ...) config row into a provider's lifecycle; providers with an SDK register their own family, the core only looks families up by the row's :family")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#defaultRowNamed" :text "--- provider rows and plugins from the gateway config ---")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#configuredRow" :text "a configured openai provider is a row: its base and keyEnv come from config, its models are claimed by the id prefix")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#rowsFromTable" :text "config.asl merges its built-in providers into every table from the process env, so built-in ids keep the settings-based default rows; config-only ids become rows ahead of them")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#pluginsFromRows" :text "a provider row may declare :redirectAfterSec; its plugin then follows that provider's 303s (a row capability, no provider-name branch)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#scalarText" :text "--- wiring config: (:gateway ... :endpoints [...] :router (:profile ...) :budget (:budgetConfig ...)) ---")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#warmState" :text "always-on endpoints start warm; a serverless provider's endpoints are reset cold by serverlessSlots")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#parseWiring" :text "every wiring key is optional: absent keys mean passthrough routing, no fleet endpoints and no budget")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#endpointStateNamed" :text "--- serverless lifecycle: (:lifecycle :provider p :family f ...) rows attach a family's lifecycle to a provider's plugin ---")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#httpLifecycle!" :text "the http family: start, status and optional stop are POSTs under the provider's base answering {\"state\": ...}; it never deploys")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#serverlessSlots" :text "a provider's endpoints follow its lifecycle: serverless slots start cold with warmupMs = coldStartMs")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#slotNamed" :text "--- route -> endpoints -> pick -> admission -> budget -> send ---")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#passthroughSlot" :text "no router profile or no matching rule: the endpoint chat chose, as an unmetered direct slot")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#routeCandidates" :text "route: router.asl orders configured endpoints; candidates whose endpoint is not configured are dropped")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#pickLoop" :text "pick by fleet spillover; an endpoint that admission or the budget refuses is recorded and the next best is picked; a cold or warming serverless endpoint is held back and waited on only when no other candidate admits")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#sendTimeout" :text "a routed endpoint runs under its own row's timeout; the chat's timeout belongs to the chat's own endpoint")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#retarget" :text "send: the chat-built request goes unchanged to its own endpoint; a routed endpoint gets its row's URL and key and the candidate model")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#withState" :text "--- charge ---")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#lifecycleRequest" :text "--- serverless start, wait and warm-up ---")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#startSlot!" :text "the first request to a cold serverless endpoint starts it through the plugin's spend-gated start; an allowed start is charged its expected cost and the endpoint goes warming")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#waiting" :text "a request that joins an endpoint already warming adds demand and waits for the same start")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#pollSlot!" :text "warming endpoints are polled through the plugin's status at most every 100 ms; warm moves the slot warm, down fails it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#slotReady" :text "a parked request sends once its endpoint admits it, keeps waiting while it warms or is full, and fails when the endpoint went away")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#carrySpend" :text "a config reload rebuilds the ledger from the new lines; spend already booked on a line id that survives the reload carries over, so editing the config never refills a cap")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/dispatch.asl#settle" :text "fleet telemetry for configured endpoints, then a budget charge priced by the endpoint; the returned text is the charge row")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/fleet.asl#" :text "Pure endpoint lifecycle, admission, bounded telemetry, scale and spillover policy.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/gateway.asl#" :text "Pure AgentScript Triple-Tier Gateway: Edge L7 routing, token bucket rate limiting, thinking-quarantine, and mesh dispatch")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-gateway/src/getRoutes.asl#" :text "GET routes of bin/asl-gateway (Handler.do_GET) as pure request -> response functions over asl-http: project and channel sync reads, health and status in ASN and JSON, voice and browser status, browser session and target lists, target and extension action polls, model list, search rendering and the fallback status")
